## 9. Caveats / known risks

### Finding: Stream deltas are live-only in v1

Affected surface:

```text
readActionEvents(...), replay:true, future graph replay/recovery, durable audit timelines
```

Why it matters:

```text
action.stream.delta events do not enter bounded retained history and disappear after live publication.
```

Smallest safe correction:

```text
Keep docs/API language as live-only opt-in stream deltas. Design retained/durable stream-delta policy separately if needed.
```

What still needs verification:

```text
Future retained/durable stream-delta branch must define storage volume, cursor semantics, retention, sampling/coalescing, and replay policy.
```

### Finding: Stream-delta publication is best-effort/no-throw

Affected surface:

```text
workerProtocolRouter stream path, prompt/output semantics, subscription listeners
```

Why it matters:

```text
A bad subscriber or mapping failure must not break prompt output, stream shaping, or final result settlement.
```

Smallest safe correction:

```text
Keep observer errors isolated and return null for unmapped/non-action request IDs.
```

What still needs verification:

```text
Future branches that move or expand stream events must preserve no-throw observer behavior unless a separate error-policy branch is approved.
```

### Finding: Default subscribers exclude stream deltas

Affected surface:

```text
existing subscribeActionEvents(...) consumers
```

Why it matters:

```text
Stream chunks may be high-volume. Delivering them by default would be a public behavior and performance surprise.
```

Smallest safe correction:

```text
Keep includeStreamDeltas defaulting false.
```

What still needs verification:

```text
Any future public API expansion should preserve backward-compatible defaults.
```

### Finding: Durable event storage and cross-process pub/sub remain excluded

Affected surface:

```text
future graph hosting, restart recovery, eventLogStoreBackend, service/process boundaries
```

Why it matters:

```text
Current events remain same-process observation. External graph/control deployment still needs a separate bridge or durable event log design.
```

Smallest safe correction:

```text
Keep eventLogStoreBackend and cross-process pub/sub in separate plan/spec branches.
```

What still needs verification:

```text
Future graph/control deployment shape and event durability requirements.
```

